      "content": "But the \"job creation\" part is always such a theoretical point, right? If we're looking at the immediate reality, the destruction of established industries and the capital flight from energy-heavy sectors seems like a much more certain outcome than some hypothetical \"green jobs\" appearing elsewhere. Can you dive deeper into the specific risks of market instability and how the sudden shift in energy policy might trigger broader economic volatility?",
